284
00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.010
So what must the agency do?

285
00:20:59.010 --> 00:21:02.138
Everything on this slide is
program design guidance,

286
00:21:02.138 --> 00:21:06.973
not a vendor or standards requirement,
condensed from a seventeen-step checklist.

287
00:21:06.973 --> 00:21:10.634
Before AD DNS retires:
choose one naming authority

288
00:21:10.634 --> 00:21:14.209
for each platform and write
down its length limit.

289
00:21:14.209 --> 00:21:19.262
For Windows, default to classic Autopilot
with Entra join and the serial number,

290
00:21:19.262 --> 00:21:24.085
and use device preparation naming only
once device association is in place.

291
00:21:24.085 --> 00:21:27.035
Inventory who registers each record today.

292
00:21:27.035 --> 00:21:29.754
Make the DHCP server the registrant,

293
00:21:29.754 --> 00:21:34.285
and lock each zone so only the
DHCP servers' keys can update it.

294
00:21:34.285 --> 00:21:40.104
Pick DHCID or TXT ownership records
once, turn off address randomization

295
00:21:40.104 --> 00:21:44.873
on agency Wi-Fi, and create
reverse zones for every DHCP scope.

296
00:21:44.873 --> 00:21:47.817
At cutover: deliver
DNS suffixes both ways,

297
00:21:47.817 --> 00:21:53.034
through DHCP options and router
announcements, and through Intune policy.

298
00:21:53.034 --> 00:21:57.228
For Entra-joined Windows, either
turn client registration off or

299
00:21:57.228 --> 00:22:01.498
accept refused attempts, but never
open zones to unsigned updates.

300
00:22:01.498 --> 00:22:04.036
Handle cloud names and servers separately.

301
00:22:04.036 --> 00:22:07.532
After: turn on scavenging
only after a quiet period,

302
00:22:07.532 --> 00:22:10.197
with lease times matched to its timers.

303
00:22:10.197 --> 00:22:14.636
Monitor duplicates, mismatched
records and devices with no record.

304
00:22:14.636 --> 00:22:18.235
Expect no AAAA records
for SLAAC addresses.

305
00:22:18.235 --> 00:22:21.498
And build certificate names from
the registered device name.

306
00:22:21.498 --> 00:22:31.235
Sources: Research brief,
Agency checklist (steps 1–17,

307
00:22:31.235 --> 00:22:44.369
all PROGRAM DESIGN GUIDANCE) and the
facts each step cites: [S1–S6, S10, S12,

308
00:22:44.369 --> 00:22:55.238
